> The selma'o BIhI consists of three words: bi'i (between), bi'o (from ...
> to ...), and mi'i (within ... of ..., in reverse order). They are
> conjunctions, not prepositions like the English words. All three can be
> optionally modified by the words "ga'o" and "ke'i", which indicate whethe=
r
> the ends of the interval are or are not included in the interval.
>
> Currently, if GAhO is used with BIhI, there must be two, one on each side=
.
